# What is tracked in this repository, and why.
#
# data/raw/ IS tracked. It is the experiment: the spectra and the hand-written
# config files beside them. It is the only thing here that cannot be
# regenerated from anything else, so it is the one thing that must be in the
# repository.
#
# data/derived/ is NOT tracked. Every file in it is reproducible from raw plus
# config by `quantify`, and the whole tree is rewritten on each run.
#
# figures/ is mostly NOT tracked, with one deliberate exception - see below.

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
.vscode/
desktop.ini

data/derived/

# The {sample}_overlay.png reference figures ARE tracked. Every other figure is
# not.
#
# Those overlays are irreplaceable *as a reference*. They can be regenerated,
# but a regenerated overlay is whatever the code happens to produce at that
# moment, which makes test_raw_plot_reference.py's comparison self-fulfilling
# and the test worthless. The stored PNG IS the baseline. Everything else under
# figures/ is ordinary build output and would commit a fresh binary blob on
# every plot run.
#
# Built up level by level on purpose. Git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so a bare `figures/` line followed by a negation would never match
# anything - the directory has to be re-included before a file inside it can
# be. The last pattern keys on the _overlay.png suffix alone: it names no
# sample, and it must not match _overlay_log.png or _overlay_baseline.png.
#
# Three levels, because figures are laid out as
# figures/<experiment>/<sample>/, one directory deeper than they once were. A
# pattern short by one component stops matching entirely: with the two-level
# rules, figures/<experiment>/<sample>/<sample>_overlay.png matched
# `figures/*/*` and the reference overlays became ignored. They stayed tracked,
# because gitignore only governs untracked files - but once untracked for any
# reason `git add` refuses them, and the baseline has no second copy.
#
# bands_all_samples.png is the one figure with no sample to live under, so it
# sits at figures/<experiment>/ and `figures/*/*` ignores it, which is right:
# it is build output like everything else that is not a reference overlay.
figures/*
!figures/*/
figures/*/*
!figures/*/*/
figures/*/*/*
!figures/*/*/*_overlay.png
